<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil declines, buyers reluctant.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil declines, buyers reluctant.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.4990)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     36.70/37.10     24.48/24.74     37.30/37.60</p>
<p> BREMEN		36.70/37.10     24.48/24.74     37.30/37.60</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    37.10/37.50     24.74/25.01     37.70/38.10</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   37.50/37.90     25.01/25.28     38.40/38.60</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   37.70/38.10     25.15/25.41     38.50/38.70</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  38.70/39.10     25.81/26.08     39.30/39.70</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices retreated on Tuesday in line with weaker futures. Demand continued to be relatively muted due to caution in the run-up to the expiry of the November futures contract. - London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
